=== HYPOTHESIS ===
# p_2f9e — The Evening Desk: Hana's Work Items at desk_b1 After 18:00

When Hana comes home from the office at 17:30, she does not dump her laptop, pen, and charger at the entry hook. Instead, she takes them directly to desk_b1 where they remain through the evening hours. The overnight sightings (00:00–06:00) show the laptop and pen at entry_hook_e1, suggesting she moves them to the entry area before bed or they rest in her work bag by the door. The charger, by contrast, is at desk_b1 overnight, consistent with it staying plugged in for the next morning. During work hours (08:00–17:30) all three items are out of the house with Hana — the four empty looks at entry_hook_e1 during 9–17h on weekdays confirm this.

This document refines the standard commuter pattern (p_a3f1) by specifying the evening resting place for Hana's work items. It directly contradicts p_d3e8 (The Entry Mess), which claims the laptop, pen, and water bottle go to entry_hook_e1 at 20:00 — the evidence shows laptop and pen at desk_b1, not the hook, during 18:00–22:00. The "mixture's worst objects" list confirms this: laptop_hana and pen_hana were predicted at entry_hook_e1 but actually found at desk_b1 three times each.

What sets this apart: p_a3f1 correctly handles the OUT_OF_HOUSE window but is silent on the evening placement (falling through to statistics, which favour entry_hook_e1). p_d3e8 actively misplaces them at the hook. This document pins them at desk_b1 for the 18–22h window.

What would refute it: the laptop, pen, or charger being sighted at entry_hook_e1 during 18–22h on a weekday; any of them at desk_b1 during 08–17h (implying Hana is working from home); or the charger at a location other than desk_b1 in the evening.

